Anyway, this wizard got lucky. My first pet kitten grew into
a large cat, killing lots of monsters for me. I picked up
the daggers and started throwing them at monsters. I polyed
the large cat in Sokoban, first into a Xorn, then into a wolf...
and ran out of /oPoly charges. Oh, well.
I had found a rather large hardware store on level 4, where I bought
a magic lamp.

As I entered the Mines to conquer it for good, I had studded leather armor,
orcish helm, low boots and BoH from sokoban.

Minetown was the normal 2-fountain small town with no sink, and it 
contained
the bones of my previous wizard. I tamed the previous pets (a large cat
and a large dog) and the murderous horse. The horse died, as did the large
dog, but my new large cat lived to be later polymorphed into a 
disenchanter.
I would later leave my wolf and disenchanter at Ludios.

I got "oRefl and a magic marker from the bones, and a small shield from one
already dead watchman. There was only 1 alive watchman in the town.
I found a leather hat and blessed the magic lamp and got
SDSM, not needing the amulet anymore.

I sacced some corpses (some I dragged from a ice box in a food store),
got Magicbane, offed some shopkeepers to get money for protection.

 From Mine's End (wine cellar) I got potions for more holy water...
and 3 luckstones. I got a throne wish from somewhere - I think I wished
for speed boots.

The rest of the game was easy. Having found "oUnchanging and a =oPC,
I succesfully polymorphed into an Arch-lich using a polytrap at one of the
quest levels. Luckily I had a +3 =oGain constitution. I never needed
a =oSD.

Polyed stuff at ludios, got a +3 hawaiian shirt and lots of spellbooks.
Nurse danced a lot in Quest Home.

After that... well, I encountered one Archon in the Plane of Fire,
and the second one in the Astral Plane. I hit him with a cockatrice
corpse. I wonder if the Archon summoned the beast?

I killed Pestilence a couple of times in a rather crude way - using
Stormy. Eventually I wisened up and used FoD.
On Astral, btw, I'd camp near the doors, having dropped the Amulet
and my BoH, so I could just cast quickly & repeatedly (almost) Magic
missile, FoD or just hack at the hordes with Stormy.
I never needed conflict - just teleported air elementals away on Air.

Oh, and I dug all of the levels to find gems. Still, not that
great score. Darn, my lawfuls and neutrals always seem to get
the best scores.


